   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I would like to install a package (<a href=\"https://github.com/tqchen/xgboost/tree/master/R-package\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/tqchen/xgboost/tree/master/R-package&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489964377000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0RnwSMV_A7f8i_ytAjcK9I\">xgboost</a> ) that is built with OpenMP enabled on OSX (Mavericks). I have already installed gcc49 via MacPorts, because the clang compiler does not support OpenMP.  The gcc is recognised in the terminal and &quot;gcc --version&quot; command prints correct compiler information.  I would like to know if there is a way to &quot;convince&quot; devtools (i.e install_github()  function ) to use this compiler instead of clang for building the package?  Or if this is not practical, how can I build the xgboost library  manually and then pack it into R package. <div><br></div><div>Thanks!</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "zgqmhQaTw_EJ",
   "from": "Timothy Bates",
   "author": "0dd6c9694b3c4809",
   "date": "2014-09-09T14:31:48Z",
   "subject": "Re: How to build package with OpenMP support on OSX (Mavericks)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">We have some instructions here which seems to work for some people... in the process of improving them, so certainly keen to leanr/share experience.<div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://openmx.psyc.virginia.edu/wiki/howto-build-openmx-source-repository\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://openmx.psyc.virginia.edu/wiki/howto-build-openmx-source-repository&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489964378000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1pDzfu7LOpeUQeCUx6T9rq\">http://openmx.psyc.virginia.edu/wiki/howto-build-openmx-source-repository</a></div><div><br></div><div>Does Simon&#39;s 4.8.2 fortran have OpenMP support?</div><div><br></div><div><div>curl -s <a href=\"http://r.research.att.com/libs/gfortran-4.8.2-darwin13.tar.bz2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://r.research.att.com/libs/gfortran-4.8.2-darwin13.tar.bz2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489964378000&amp;usg=AOvVaw220W-So9wpBYllYrpZQ9yB\">http://r.research.att.com/libs/gfortran-4.8.2-darwin13.tar.bz2</a> | sudo tar fxj - -C /<br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><br></div><br>On Monday, September 8, 2014 1:48:44 PM UTC+1, damjan dvorsek wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I would like to install a package (<a href=\"https://github.com/tqchen/xgboost/tree/master/R-package\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/tqchen/xgboost/tree/master/R-package&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792489964378000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0XTijMN3kdq30Kel6FPB-2\">xgboost</a> ) that is built with OpenMP enabled on OSX (Mavericks). I have already installed gcc49 via MacPorts, because the clang compiler does not support OpenMP.  The gcc is recognised in the terminal and &quot;gcc --version&quot; command prints correct compiler information.  I would like to know if there is a way to &quot;convince&quot; devtools (i.e install_github()  function ) to use this compiler instead of clang for building the package?  Or if this is not practical, how can I build the xgboost library  manually and then pack it into R package. <div><br></div><div>Thanks!</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
